Here's a clean, interactive image comparison slider in HTML:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0"/>
  <title>Image Comparison Slider</title>
  <style>
    * {
      margin: 0;
      padding: 0;
      box-sizing: border-box;
    }

    body {
      min-height: 100vh;
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
      background: #1a1a2e;
      font-family: 'Segoe UI', sans-serif;
      padding: 20px;
    }

    h1 {
      color: #e0e0e0;
      margin-bottom: 10px;
      font-size: 2rem;
      letter-spacing: 1px;
    }

    p.subtitle {
      color: #888;
      margin-bottom: 30px;
      font-size: 0.95rem;
    }

    .comparison-container {
      position: relative;
      width: 100%;
      max-width: 800px;
      height: 500px;
      overflow: hidden;
      border-radius: 12px;
      box-shadow: 0 20px 60px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5);
      cursor: col-resize;
      user-select: none;
    }

    /* BEFORE image (bottom layer, full width) */
    .img-before,
    .img-after {
      position: absolute;
      top: 0;
      left: 0;
      width: 100%;
      height: 100%;
      object-fit: cover;
      display: block;
    }

    /* AFTER image (top layer, clipped) */
    .img-after-wrapper {
      position: absolute;
      top: 0;
      left: 0;
      width: 50%;
      height: 100%;
      overflow: hidden;
    }

    .img-after {
      width: 800px; /* match max-width of container */
      max-width: none;
    }

    /* Divider line */
    .divider {
      position: absolute;
      top: 0;
      left: 50%;
      transform: translateX(-50%);
      width: 3px;
      height: 100%;
      background: #fff;
      box-shadow: 0 0 10px rgba(0,0,0,0.5);
      z-index: 10;
    }

    /* Handle circle */
    .handle {
      position: absolute;
      top: 50%;
      left: 50%;
      transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
      width: 50px;
      height: 50px;
      background: #fff;
      border-radius: 50%;
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
      box-shadow: 0 2px 15px rgba(0,0,0,0.4);
      z-index: 11;
      font-size: 18px;
      color: #333;
    }

    .handle::before {
      content: "◀";
      position: absolute;
      left: 6px;
      font-size: 12px;
      color: #555;
    }

    .handle::after {
      content: "▶";
      position: absolute;
      right: 6px;
      font-size: 12px;
      color: #555;
    }

    /* Labels */
    .label {
      position: absolute;
      top: 15px;
      padding: 5px 12px;
      background: rgba(0,0,0,0.55);
      color: #fff;
      border-radius: 20px;
      font-size: 0.8rem;
      font-weight: 600;
      letter-spacing: 1px;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      z-index: 5;
      pointer-events: none;
    }

    .label-before {
      right: 15px;
    }

    .label-after {
      left: 15px;
    }

    .instructions {
      color: #666;
      margin-top: 20px;
      font-size: 0.85rem;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>

  <h1>Image Comparison</h1>
  <p class="subtitle">Drag the slider to compare before &amp; after</p>

  <div class="comparison-container" id="container">

    <!-- BEFORE image -->
    <img
      class="img-before"
      src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?w=800&q=80"
      alt="Before"
    />

    <!-- AFTER image (clipped) -->
    <div class="img-after-wrapper" id="afterWrapper">
      <img
        class="img-after"
        src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1501854140801-50d01698950b?w=800&q=80"
        alt="After"
      />
    </div>

    <!-- Labels -->
    <div class="label label-before">Before</div>
    <div class="label label-after">After</div>

    <!-- Divider + Handle -->
    <div class="divider" id="divider">
      <div class="handle"></div>
    </div>

  </div>

  <p class="instructions">🖱️ Click and drag — or touch and swipe on mobile</p>

  <script>
    const container  = document.getElementById('container');
    const divider    = document.getElementById('divider');
    const afterWrapper = document.getElementById('afterWrapper');

    let isDragging = false;

    function setPosition(x) {
      const rect = container.getBoundingClientRect();
      let offsetX = x - rect.left;

      // Clamp between 0 and container width
      offsetX = Math.max(0, Math.min(offsetX, rect.width));

      const percent = (offsetX / rect.width) * 100;

      divider.style.left       = percent + '%';
      afterWrapper.style.width = percent + '%';
    }

    // Mouse events
    container.addEventListener('mousedown', (e) => {
      isDragging = true;
      setPosition(e.clientX);
    });

    window.addEventListener('mousemove', (e) => {
      if (!isDragging) return;
      setPosition(e.clientX);
    });

    window.addEventListener('mouseup', () => {
      isDragging = false;
    });

    // Touch events
    container.addEventListener('touchstart', (e) => {
      isDragging = true;
      setPosition(e.touches[0].clientX);
    }, { passive: true });

    window.addEventListener('touchmove', (e) => {
      if (!isDragging) return;
      setPosition(e.touches[0].clientX);
    }, { passive: true });

    window.addEventListener('touchend', () => {
      isDragging = false;
    });
  </script>

</body>
</html>
```

## How It Works

### Structure
- **Two images** are stacked on top of each other using `position: absolute`
- The **"After" image** is wrapped in a `div` whose width is clipped dynamically
- A **divider line** with a circular **handle** sits between the two images

### Interaction
| Event | Action |
|-------|--------|
| `mousedown` | Start dragging |
| `mousemove` | Update slider position |
| `mouseup` | Stop dragging |
| `touchstart/move/end` | Same behavior on mobile |

### Customization
- 🖼️ **Swap images** — replace the `src` URLs with your own images
- 🎨 **Change colors** — modify the `background` in `body` and handle styles
- 📐 **Resize** — adjust `.comparison-container` height/max-width
- 🏷️ **Labels** — edit the "Before" / "After" text in the HTML

